good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8238b0bd-1624-4cbd-8a34-fc44254ec8eb_1080x1080.jpeg\" width=\"1080\" height=\"1080\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/8238b0bd-1624-4cbd-8a34-fc44254ec8eb_1080x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1080,&quot;width&quot;:1080,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:268571,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Power &amp; Pause Retreat by Subba Sattvic and Erin Lee, Ubud Bali&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Power &amp; Pause Retreat by Subba Sattvic and Erin Lee, Ubud Bali&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/i/196276565?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8238b0bd-1624-4cbd-8a34-fc44254ec8eb_1080x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"Power &amp; Pause Retreat by Subba Sattvic and Erin Lee, Ubud Bali\" title=\"Power &amp; Pause Retreat by Subba Sattvic and Erin Lee, Ubud Bali\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GMsm!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8238b0bd-1624-4cbd-8a34-fc44254ec8eb_1080x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GMsm!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8238b0bd-1624-4cbd-8a34-fc44254ec8eb_1080x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GMsm!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8238b0bd-1624-4cbd-8a34-fc44254ec8eb_1080x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GMsm!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8238b0bd-1624-4cbd-8a34-fc44254ec8eb_1080x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><h4><strong>Free Online Intro Session</strong></h4><p>Register your interest here to join our free online introductory session to learn about the framework that we will be sharing during the program.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://beingme.com.sg/power-and-pause&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Intro Session Details&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;button-wrapper&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary button-wrapper\" href=\"https://beingme.com.sg/power-and-pause\"><span>Intro Session Details</span></a></p><div><hr></div><p></p>",
  "body_text": "When we think about wisdom, we may associate it with knowledge, intelligence, or years of experience. \n\nFrom the perspective of mindfulness, wisdom — or paññā — is something much more profound.\n\nWisdom is the ability to see things clearly.\n\nIt is the capacity to understand what leads to suffering and what leads away from it. \n\nIt is recognising how fear, attachment, craving, and resistance shape our experience, and how often we create additional (and often unnecessary) struggle by holding on too tightly to what we want life to be.\n\nIn today’s world, we are surrounded by more information than ever before. We have access to endless opinions, perspectives, and advice. Yet despite all this knowledge, many of us still feel overwhelmed, reactive, and dissatisfied. Information alone does not guarantee wisdom.\n\nWisdom begins with pausing.\n\nWhen we slow down and pay attention, we start to observe our thoughts, emotions, and habits more clearly. \n\nWe notice what is helpful and what is not. We learn that not every thought deserves to be believed, and not every emotion needs to dictate our response.\n\nOver time, wisdom reveals itself in ordinary moments: pausing before reacting in anger, letting go of the need to be right, or accepting that change is simply part of life.\n\nWisdom is not about becoming someone who is special or highly-regarded. \n\nIt is learning to meet life as it is, with greater clarity, understanding, and ease.\n\n---\n\nMeditation Practice:\n\nOver 30-31 May 2026, the TAP community created the conditions for cultivating wisdom through a mindfulness meditation practice. We closed the session with reading a poem by Ullie-Kaye. \n\nTap Play to Practice Together:\n\nThis post is free for 4 weeks, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. Upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.\n\nShare\n\n---\n\nThe Wholehearted Woman Retreat\n\nA five-day mindfulness retreat into quiet wisdom and the light within\n\n1-5 October 2026\nSiem Reap, Cambodia\n\nLed by Erin Lee\n\nJoin Erin at Angkor Wat\n\n---\n\nPower & Pause Retreat\n\nA high-touch program supported by structured processes, guided practices, and reflective assignments\n\n24 - 28 September 2026\nUbud, Bali\n\nLed by Subba Sattvic and Erin Lee\n\nFree Online Intro Session\n\nRegister your interest here to join our free online introductory session to learn about the framework that we will be sharing during the program.\n\nIntro Session Details\n\n---",
